<!-- #region ls -->

| x | y | x² | xy |
|--:|--:|--:|--:|
| 1.2 | 4 | 1.44 | 4.8 |
| 2.3 | 5.6 | 5.29 | 12.88 |
| 3.1 | 7.9 | 9.61 | 24.49 |
| 3.4 | 8 | 11.56 | 27.2 |
| 4 | 10.1 | 16 | 40.4 |
| 4.6 | 10.4 | 21.16 | 47.84 |
| 5.5 | 12 | 30.25 | 66 |
| **24.1** | **58** | **95.31** | **223.61** |

$$ \begin{aligned} a &= \frac{n\sum xy - \sum x\sum y}{n\sum x^2 - (\sum x)^2} = \frac{7(223.61) - (24.1)(58)}{7(95.31) - (24.1)^2} = \frac{1565.27 - 1397.8}{667.17 - 580.81} = \frac{167.47}{86.36} = 1.94 \\ b &= \bar y - a\bar x = 8.2857 - 1.9392 \times 3.4429 = 1.61 \end{aligned} $$

**Line: ŷ = 1.94x + 1.61.** The data was made from y = 2x + 1.5 plus noise, and the fit recovers it closely. SSE = 0.974, TSS = 47.369, so R² = 1 − 0.974/47.369 = **0.98**: the line explains 98% of the variation.

