<p class="fig-cap">Seven steps from w = 0 on f(w) = (w − 3)². Too small: crawls. Large: overshoots back and forth but still settles. Too large: every step overshoots further and the cost grows.</p>

<!-- #endregion lr-cases -->
<!-- #region gd-lr -->

**Iteration 1** (w = 0, b = 0):

| x | y | ŷ = wx + b | e = ŷ − y | e·x |
|:-:|:-:|--:|--:|--:|
| 1 | 3 | 0 | −3 | −3 |
| 2 | 4 | 0 | −4 | −8 |
| 4 | 8 | 0 | −8 | −32 |
|  |  | **Σ** | **−15** | **−43** |

$$ \begin{aligned} \frac{\partial J}{\partial w} &= \tfrac{2}{n}\textstyle\sum e\,x = \tfrac{2}{3}(-43) = -28.6667, &w &\leftarrow 0 - 0.05(-28.6667) = \mathbf{1.4333} \\ \frac{\partial J}{\partial b} &= \tfrac{2}{n}\textstyle\sum e = \tfrac{2}{3}(-15) = -10, &b &\leftarrow 0 - 0.05(-10) = \mathbf{0.5} \end{aligned} $$

**Iteration 2** (w = 1.4333, b = 0.5):

| x | y | ŷ = wx + b | e = ŷ − y | e·x |
|:-:|:-:|--:|--:|--:|
| 1 | 3 | 1.9333 | −1.0667 | −1.0667 |
| 2 | 4 | 3.3667 | −0.6333 | −1.2667 |
| 4 | 8 | 6.2333 | −1.7667 | −7.0667 |
|  |  | **Σ** | **−3.4667** | **−9.4** |

$$ \begin{aligned} \frac{\partial J}{\partial w} &= \tfrac{2}{n}\textstyle\sum e\,x = \tfrac{2}{3}(-9.4) = -6.2667, &w &\leftarrow 1.4333 - 0.05(-6.2667) = \mathbf{1.7467} \\ \frac{\partial J}{\partial b} &= \tfrac{2}{n}\textstyle\sum e = \tfrac{2}{3}(-3.4667) = -2.3111, &b &\leftarrow 0.5 - 0.05(-2.3111) = \mathbf{0.6156} \end{aligned} $$

MSE: 29.6667 at the start → 0.1923 after two iterations. (The least-squares answer for this data is w = 1.7143, b = 1; gradient descent is walking towards it.)

<!-- #endregion gd-lr -->
<!-- #region nonconvex -->

<svg class="fig" viewBox="0 0 520 280" role="img" aria-label="A non-convex function with a local and a global minimum">
<line class="ax" x1="36" y1="250" x2="506" y2="250"/>
<line class="ax" x1="36" y1="250" x2="36" y2="12"/>
